; Theme colors for the inlay hints of Visual Studio's LSP client (Fonts and Colors > Inlay Hints - Types / Inlay Hints - Parameters).
; Visual Studio 18 files its Dark entries for these items under the Output Window category, so Kotlin and Java editors
; fall back to the light defaults (#686868 on #E6E6E6). These keys add them to the editor's category
; (Text Editor MEF Items, {75a05685-00a8-4ded-bae5-e7a50bfa929a}) with the values Visual Studio meant for Dark, which
; also match C# and C++ inline hints. Dark-based themes fall back to Dark; Dark (Extra Contrast) gets its own inlay hint colors.
; Blob: int32 length, int32 version 11, int32 category count, category GUID, int32 item count, then per item an
; int32-prefixed UTF-8 name and background/foreground as type 1 (raw) + R,G,B,A. Checked by InlayHintTests.ThemeColors.
[$RootKey$\Themes\{1ded0138-47ce-435e-84ef-9ec1f439b749}\Vistudio Text Editor MEF Items]
